## Why 76?

Because the site lives at [000000076.xyz](https://000000076.xyz/), and the grove began with 76 hand-tended Eleventy themes. It continues to grow with ports, remixes, and originals. Some are ports of Hugo, Zola, Jekyll, WordPress, Ghost, and Astro themes reworked for 11ty. Others explore CSS frameworks: Blades, Bootstrap, Tailwind, Chota, Sakura, Tacit, MVP, μ, and more.

## Who

Built by [Adam DJ Brett](https://adamdjbrett.com), educator, curriculum designer, and enthusiastic port-and-remix tinkerer. Every theme in this directory lives under [github.com/adamdjbrett](https://github.com/adamdjbrett?tab=repositories&q=11ty-) with the prefix `11ty-`.

## Built with

- **[Eleventy (11ty)](https://www.11ty.dev/)** — the friendlier static-site generator.
- **[Build Awesome One](https://buildawesome.one/) starter** — declutters project root by hiding config in `.build/`.
- **[Blades CSS](https://blades.ninja/)** — the classless-first CSS kit that ships with Build Awesome.
- **[Eleventy Screenshot API](https://github.com/11ty/api-screenshot)** — captures the theme previews, which are stored locally as WebP files.
- A warm citrus overlay (`css/oranges.css`) — the only custom stylesheet on top.

## Use a theme

1. Find a theme you like on the [themes page](/themes/) or by [tag](/tags/).
2. Click through to its detail page and grab the GitHub repo link.
3. `git clone` it, `cd .build && npm install && npm start`, and you're editing.

## Contribute

Spotted a bug? Have a theme you'd like to see ported? Open an issue on any of the [repos](https://github.com/adamdjbrett?tab=repositories&q=11ty-).
